      "title": "Sessional Instructor",
      "description": "Sessional Instructor - OPMA 415 LEC 01 & LEC 02, Winter 2027, Haskayne School of Business in \n            \n                Calgary,\n            \n            \n                \n                \n                    AB,\n                \n            \n            Canada Skip to main content Menu Careers Home See All Jobs Candidate Information Total Rewards at UCalgary Workplace Diversity and Inclusion Indigenous Candidates Accessibility and Accommodation Application FAQ's Apply Now Require Authentication must be enabled to output referral button. Sessional Instructor - OPMA 415 LEC 01 & LEC 02, Winter 2027, Haskayne School of Business Job ID: 38911 Location: Main Campus Updated October 16, 2026 Apply Now Share: Share on Twitter share to twitter Share on Facebook share to facebook Share on LinkedIn share to linkedin Share with Email Loading job Back to Search Results Previous Opportunity Next Opportunity We would like to take this opportunity to acknowledge the traditional territories of the people of the Treaty 7 region in Southern Alberta. The City of Calgary is also home to Métis Nation within Alberta (Nose Hill Métis District 5 and Elbow Métis District 6). Description The Haskayne School of Business at the University of Calgary invites applications for a Sessional Instructor to teach Winter 2027 OPMA 415 (Prescriptive Models in Business Analytics). Classes in the Winter 2027 semester run from January 11 to April 13, 2027. Registrar Scheduled Exams will take place between April 16 to April 27, 2027, if applicable. OPMA 415 (Prescriptive Models in Business Analytics) LEC 01 Tuesday 6:00pm - 8:45pm TUT 01 : Tuesday 5:00pm - 5:50pm LEC 02 Friday 11:00am - 1:45pm TUT 02 : Friday 10:00am - 10:50am The Calendar description of the course: \"Identification of data requirements for analytical decision-making. Case studies used throughout to develop insight for decision making while dealing with incomplete and ambiguous data. Introduction to VBA-enabled spreadsheet modelling to design and implement optimization models without/with uncertainty as well as advanced Monte Carlo simulation.\" Qualifications Graduate degree (MBA, MSc, DBA or PhD) or recent work experience in a relevant field is required. Previous post-secondary teaching experience of a quantitative course with statistics and Linear Programming, and the use of Excel is required. Affinity to teach quantitative solution techniques with the use of VBA in Excel is required. Demonstrate the ability to foster student engagement at the undergraduate level. Located in or near Calgary for the in-person delivery of the course is required. To apply, please submit your application online via the 'Apply Now' link and address your cover letter to the attention of Marco Bijvank, Area Chair, Operations and Supply Chain Management . DO NOT email your application directly to Marco Bijvank. In support of your application, please provide the following in your application package: A current CV containing a discussion of relevant teaching and professional experience. Previous teaching evaluations, if applicable. Names of three references. Any additional information that you may have to strengthen your application and assist in the selection process. Please be aware that the application process only allows for four attachments, which may require you to merge documents. The application deadline is October 30, 2026 . Please note that consideration of applicants may begin before the application deadline. Incomplete applications will not be considered. While we accept all applications for this vacancy, we may have candidates with the right of first refusal as per Article 23.12.1 of the University of Calgary Faculty Association Collective Agreement. The amount of remuneration is calculated according to the Collective Agreement, Schedule B. Please see the Faculty Association website at http://www.ucalgary.ca/TUCFA for further information regarding conditions of employment and r