      "description": "Sessional Instructor - MKTG 437 LEC 01, Winter 2027, Haskayne School of Business in \n            \n                Calgary,\n            \n            \n                \n                \n                    AB,\n                \n            \n            Canada Skip to main content Menu Careers Home See All Jobs Candidate Information Total Rewards at UCalgary Workplace Diversity and Inclusion Indigenous Candidates Accessibility and Accommodation Application FAQ's Apply Now Require Authentication must be enabled to output referral button. Sessional Instructor - MKTG 437 LEC 01, Winter 2027, Haskayne School of Business Job ID: 38950 Location: Main Campus Updated October 20, 2026 Apply Now Share: Share on Twitter share to twitter Share on Facebook share to facebook Share on LinkedIn share to linkedin Share with Email Loading job Back to Search Results Previous Opportunity Next Opportunity We would like to take this opportunity to acknowledge the traditional territories of the people of the Treaty 7 region in Southern Alberta. The City of Calgary is also home to Métis Nation within Alberta (Nose Hill Métis District 5 and Elbow Métis District 6). Description The Haskayne School of Business at the University of Calgary invites applications for a Sessional Instructor to teach Winter 2027 MKTG 437 L01 (Marketing Analytics). Classes in the Winter 2027 semester run from January 11 to April 13, 2027. Registrar Scheduled Exams will take place between April 16 to April 27, 2027, if applicable. MKTG 437 (Marketing Analytics) LEC 01 Tuesday/Thursday 2:00pm - 3:15pm The calendar description of the course: \"Introduction to data-driven marketing strategies, covering market research, marketing mix modelling, segmentation, social media analytics, and data analysis techniques. Course uses R and involves hands-on experience with real-world databases.\" Qualifications MBA degree or equivalent and work experience in marketing and/or analytics are desirable. Previ